<!--
  The adaptive icon's foreground: the Student Union's own SU monogram.

  Traced from `art/su.png`, the master the white `drawable-nodpi/logo_su.png`
  on the welcome screen, the pass and the profile also comes from — so the
  launcher and the app are showing one mark rather than two drawings of it. The
  monogram is straight-edged by construction, so it is stored as polygons: the
  trace was run with curve fitting off and the result reduced to 31 vertices,
  which is the mark exactly rather than an approximation of it.

  **The `MFU` that rides up the right-hand side of the full logo is not here.**
  Its cap height is about a fifteenth of the monogram's, which at a 48dp
  launcher icon is under a pixel and a half — three letters of grey mud beside
  a mark that reads fine on its own. The full lockup, MFU and wordmark
  included, is what `logo_su.png` is for, and that one is only ever drawn
  large.

  Lime rather than the brand's white. White is correct on the pass, which is
  paper; the icon sits on the app's own ground, and `Palette.Accent` is what
  every other lit thing in this app is — the scan ring, the CTAs, the ticks.
  An icon in the accent says which app this is from across a home screen.

  Sized so the furthest vertex sits 30.5dp from centre: 57dp across, inside the
  66dp safe circle with room to spare, and still full enough not to read as a
  logo someone forgot to scale up. It doubles as the `monochrome` layer, where
  the system replaces this fill with the theme's own tint.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- The wedge at the top of the U — a separate shape in the master, not a hole. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFC6F16C"
        android:pathData="M64.14,47.32L64.14,36.8L55.93,41.46L55.96,42.91Z" />
    <!-- The S and the U, which interlock into one outline. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFC6F16C"
